nora_csm: Heads-up: BlinkApp onboarding — iOS SDK is firing 6-8 embedding requests on app cold-open (one per active view) and we're seeing 429s spiking within 90s of release. they report user signups stuck until embeddings finish.
ben_cs_eng: account? hosted or dedicated? any error payloads?
nora_csm: acct: blink-prod, Hosted. customer pasted error: `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\",\"detail\":\"too many concurrent embedding requests\"}`. No Retry-After.
ashley_sre: sounds like concurrent-per-tenant concurrency cap on /v1/embeddings. mobile apps often fan out when restoring state. two quick mitigations: 1) client debounce/pool embeddings per session 2) connection keepalive so multiple requests reuse sockets (lower connection churn counts).
tang_devex: agree. sending a tiny iOS snippet to centralize token + queue embeds. recommend hold max concurrency to 2 and use FIFO queue.
ben_cs_eng: can you paste snippet? we'll share with Blink before call. also we can give them a short quota bump while they roll code.
tang_devex: Swift pseudocode: ```swift
// AppDelegate or SDK singleton
class EmbedManager {
  static let shared = EmbedManager()
  private var token: String? = nil
  private var tokenExpiry: Date = .distantPast
  private let queue = DispatchQueue(label: "embed-queue", qos: .userInitiated)
  private var sem = DispatchSemaphore(value: 2) // max 2 concurrent

  func getToken(completion: @escaping (String?) -> Void) {
    if Date() < tokenExpiry, let t = token { completion(t); return }
    // fetch ephemeral token once
    URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: URL(string: "https://auth.blinkapp.com/ephemeral")!) { data, _, _ in
      guard let d = data, let s = String(data: d, encoding: .utf8) else { completion(nil); return }
      self.token = s
      self.tokenExpiry = Date().addingTimeInterval(45)
      completion(s)
    }.resume()
  }

  func embed(text: String, completion: @escaping (Result<Data, Error>) -> Void) {
    queue.async {
      let jitter = Double.random(in: 0...0.2)
      Thread.sleep(forTimeInterval: jitter)
      self.sem.wait()
      defer { self.sem.signal() }
      self.getToken { token in
        guard let token = token else { completion(.failure(NSError())); return }
        var req = URLRequest(url: URL(string: "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/embeddings")!)
        req.httpMethod = "POST"
        req.addValue("Bearer \(token)", forHTTPHeaderField: "Authorization")
        req.addValue("blink-ios", forHTTPHeaderField: "x-sdk")
        // include per-install id to help us correlate
        req.addValue(UIDevice.current.identifierForVendor?.uuidString ?? "-", forHTTPHeaderField: "x-install-id")
        req.httpBody = try? JSONEncoder().encode(["input": text])
        URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: req) { data, resp, err in
          if let http = resp as? HTTPURLResponse, http.statusCode == 429 {
            // optional client-side backoff retry
          }
          completion(.success(data ?? Data()))
        }.resume()
      }
    }
  }
}
```
